; Export definition — shared by all six build variants.
;
; There is deliberately NO `LIBRARY` line. It would stamp one fixed module name
; into every variant's export directory, and the variants ship under six
; different filenames; ld instead takes the name from the output file, so each
; DLL describes itself. Nothing binds against that field anyway — the exe's
; import table names the DLL it wants, and resolves BlackboxEntry by ordinal #1.
;
; pmc_log is exported by name for ASI plugins to resolve via GetProcAddress. All
; three exports are present in EVERY variant: the quiet builds
; (-DPMC_DISABLE_LOG_STACK) back pmc_log/pmc_log_flush with inert stubs rather
; than dropping them, so a plugin that has found the module always finds the
; symbol, whichever variant is installed.
EXPORTS
    BlackboxEntry @1
    pmc_log
    pmc_log_flush
